# Plans / scratch (mirrors acdp-rs convention)
#
# `plans/<feature>.md` stays ignored: those are per-run working documents, and
# committing them would put in-flight planning churn into the repo's history.
#
# `plans/cross-repo/` is DELIBERATELY TRACKED, and the exception is load-bearing
# rather than cosmetic. `/plan`'s cross-repo handoff writes the design for
# another repo HERE (writing into a sibling repo needs a human gate; reading one
# never does) and then files an issue THERE linking back to a GitHub blob URL.
# While the whole of `plans/` was ignored, that URL pointed at a file that was
# never committed, so every such link 404'd -- the handoff silently produced a
# pointer to nothing. acdp-rs#273 was filed that way and had to carry its design
# inline instead. A cross-repo plan is a contract with another repo, not scratch.
#
# NOTE the `plans/*` + negation form: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a bare `plans/` makes `!plans/cross-repo/` unreachable. The
# directory itself must stay un-excluded for the negation to be reachable at all.
plans/*
!plans/cross-repo/
temp/


.claude/
memory/
CLAUDE.md

# Lane scratch (untracked, never committed)
# Root-anchored deliberately: an unanchored `PROGRESS.md` would also hide a
# future crates/*/PROGRESS.md, which is not what this covers.
/PROGRESS.md
/.drive.lock
